; ============================================================
; TITLE:    Color Wheel
; CATEGORY: Generative Art & Colour
; LEVEL:    Beginner
; TAGS:     color, RGB, FILLED, wedges, primary colors
; SUMMARY:  Paints a twelve part artist's color wheel from a list of RGB colors.
; ============================================================
;
; WHAT IT DOES
;   Paints twelve slices like a pie, going round from red through
;   yellow, green, blue and purple and back to red. The three
;   primary colors of light (red, green and blue) are four slices
;   apart. A white circle in the middle turns the pie into a ring.
;
; HOW TO USE
;   Press Run. Change the colors in the list at the bottom, or the
;   radius in SLICE.
;
; CONCEPTS YOU WILL LEARN
;   * colors as [red green blue] lists from 0 to 255
;   * FILLED to paint the inside of a shape
;   * FOREACH to visit every color in a list
;   * a big DOT to paint a circle
;
; THINGS TO TRY
;   * Swap the order of the colors. Does the wheel still look smooth?
;   * Make the white hole in the middle bigger or smaller.
;   * Make a wheel of 6 slices of 60 degrees.
; ============================================================

; SLICE paints one 30 degree slice in a color. The turtle starts in
; the middle facing the slice's left edge, and comes back to the
; middle afterward.
to slice :color
  filled :color [
    forward 220
    right 90
    ; 30 small steps and 1 degree turns walk along the rim. The step
    ; is the circle's length (2 x 3.14 x 220) shared out over 360.
    repeat 30 [forward 3.84 right 1]
    right 90
    forward 220
  ]
end

; WHEEL paints one slice for each color, turning 30 degrees each time.
to wheel :colors
  penup home
  ; A white pen draws thin white lines between the slices.
  pendown setpencolor 7 setpensize 3
  foreach :colors [
    setheading 30 * (# - 1)
    slice ?
  ]
end

clearscreen hideturtle
setbackground [235 235 235]
wheel [[255 0 0] [255 128 0] [255 255 0] [128 255 0]
       [0 255 0] [0 255 128] [0 255 255] [0 128 255]
       [0 0 255] [128 0 255] [255 0 255] [255 0 128]]
; The hole in the middle: one big white dot.
setpencolor 7
setpensize 180
dot [0 0]
